{
  "id": "page.interview.coding-errors",
  "title": "Dictionary pattern B - Count errors by code",
  "summary": "Coding / Python / Dictionaries / Grouping and state",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.prompt",
      "title": "Question",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.question",
          "text": "Given error-code strings, return the frequency of each code. How is this the same pattern as grouping rows?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.reasoning",
      "title": "Reasoning",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.reasoning-points",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            "Use the code as key.",
            "Start an unseen key at zero.",
            "Increment for each observation.",
            "Specify whether case and missing values should be normalized upstream."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.answer",
      "title": "Answer / mental model",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.explanation",
          "text": "The dictionary key is now the error code and the accumulator is an integer, not a list. The loop still finds a key and updates its state."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.example",
      "title": "Example",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "def count_errors(codes):\n    counts = {}\n    for code in codes:\n        counts[code] = counts.get(code, 0) + 1\n    return counts"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.alternatives",
      "title": "Alternative / tradeoff",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.alternative-0",
          "text": "Counter expresses frequency counting directly; the manual version reveals the interview pattern."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.alternative-code-0",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "from collections import Counter\n\ndef count_errors_alternative(codes):\n    return dict(Counter(codes))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.complexity",
      "title": "Complexity / tradeoff",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.cost",
          "text": "Expected O(n) time and O(k) output space for k distinct codes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.trap",
      "title": "Common mistake / trap",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.trap-note",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "Watch for this",
          "text": "Reinitializing the count to zero inside every iteration loses earlier observations."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.followup",
      "title": "Follow-up",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.followups",
          "items": [
            "How would you count by (service, error_code) instead?"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.intent",
      "title": "Interviewer intent",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "id": "page.interview.coding-errors.intent-points",
          "items": [
            "Recognize the same keyed-accumulator pattern.",
            "Explain defaults and updates."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
